\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces High-level layered architecture. Dialogue interpretation and symbolic grounding provide parallel inputs to the planning layer. The chatbot layer also consumes symbolic scene context. The planner proposes structured skill plans, while the execution layer validates and dispatches skills before returning feedback for supervision.}}{11}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Runtime message and responsibility sequence from user input to spoken response. The colour coding follows Figure~\ref {fig:layered-architecture}: dialogue components are blue, grounding and evidence are orange, planning is green, and execution is purple.}}{12}{figure.caption.12}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Grounded-context pipeline. Scene and KB evidence are projected by a grounded perception helper into a compact \code {grounded_context} for \code {chatbot_llm} and \code {planner_llm}. Skills receive planner-approved arguments through execution, while also retaining access to raw scene and KB evidence for live requery and validation before reporting outcomes.}}{20}{figure.caption.17}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Full-stack implementation of the NAO ROS4HRI bridge. Dialogue components are blue, grounding and evidence components orange, planning components green, execution components purple, and skills or adapters neutral grey. Dashed red boxes denote future extensions rather than claims about the implemented runtime.}}{27}{figure.caption.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Internal \code {chatbot_llm} path. The node owns semantic interpretation and candidate planner metadata, but not plan construction, dispatch, or speech execution.}}{29}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Internal \code {planner_llm} path, from admitted request through validated plan envelope and goal-keyed supervision.}}{29}{figure.caption.22}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The \code {nao_orchestrator} admission and execution boundaries. All effects cross deterministic validation and retain goal and plan lineage.}}{31}{figure.caption.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Combined perception and symbolic-grounding pipeline. Compact projections serve dialogue and planning, while raw and fresh evidence remains at its owning seam.}}{32}{figure.caption.24}%
